  "term": "hearing aid",
  "definition": "A hearing aid is a device used by some people who still have limited usable hearing in one ear, including alongside a cochlear implant in the other ear. In this context, adding a hearing aid to the nonimplanted ear may improve hearing in noise, sound localization, and everyday communication.",
