      "reasons": [
        "The definition states “some people who still have limited usable hearing in one ear,” but the provided packet only discusses a specific group: unilateral cochlear implant listeners with limited hearing in the unimplanted (contralateral) ear. The definition’s first sentence is therefore broader than what the packet supports.",
        "The field specified is “cognition,” but the packet evaluates audiological outcomes (speech perception in noise, lateralization) and subjective questionnaires; it provides no support that this belongs to cognition as such.",
        "The claim about improving “everyday communication” is only indirectly supported: the packet reports subjective preference for hearing aids in “spatial awareness and communication domains,” not an observed everyday communication improvement."
